### Open a new order for customer 1 (seeded)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": 1
}

> {% client.global.set("orderNo", response.body.orderNumber); %}

### Add two coffee mugs (product 1)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/orders/{{orderNo}}/lines
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "quantity": 2
}

### Add one notebook (product 3)
POST http://localhost:8081/api/orders/{{orderNo}}/lines
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 3,
  "quantity": 1
}

### Place the order: status O becomes P
PATCH http://localhost:8081/api/orders/{{orderNo}}/place

### Read the order back
GET http://localhost:8081/api/orders/{{orderNo}}

### Adding a line after placing is rejected with 409
POST http://localhost:8081/api/orders/{{orderNo}}/lines
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": 1,
  "quantity": 1
}

### An unknown order is 404
GET http://localhost:8081/api/orders/ORD-999999

### A write made by the sync process: LAST_UPD_BY becomes SYNC instead of APP,
### which is what the middleware filters on to stop sync loops (see #14)
PATCH http://localhost:8081/api/orders/{{orderNo}}/cancel
X-Updated-By: SYNC
